[7:0]: SCHED_INFO (Schedule information)

Every bit in this 8 bit register indicates scheduling for that microframe.

Bit 0 indicates scheduling for 1st microframe and bit 7 indicates scheduling for 8th microframe in that frame.

A value of 8'b11111111 indicates that the corresponding interrupt channel is scheduled to issue a token every microframe in that frame. A value of 8'b10101010 indicates that the corresponding interrupt channel is scheduled to issue a token every alternate microframe starting with second microframe. Note that this field is applicable only for periodic (Isochronous and Interrupt) channels.</description>
